---
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';

const steps = [
  ['Accept', 'One io_uring ring per core with multishot accept. <code>SO_REUSEPORT</code> lets the kernel spread connections across cores, so no core waits on another.'],
  ['Handshake', 'rustls runs the TLS handshake, then hands the session keys to the kernel. After that the kernel encrypts records in place and liamd never copies ciphertext.'],
  ['Route', 'Hostnames resolve through a perfect hash and paths through a radix tree. <code>liam build</code> compiles both from your config, so a lookup touches a few cache lines.'],
  ['Respond', 'Static responses go out with <code>sendfile</code> from the page cache, already compressed, with no copy through userspace. Dynamic routes use a pooled keep-alive proxy or a Wasm handler compiled ahead of time and run on the same core.'],
  ['Log', 'Structured log lines go to a per-core ring buffer and are flushed off the hot path. A slow disk or a slow collector never slows a response.'],
];
---

<Section id="hotpath" eyebrow="Hot path" title="What happens to one request.">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Speed comes from skipping work. Each step below does less than a conventional server does at the same point, and
    the static path does no heap allocation.
  </Fragment>
  <ol class="path">
    {
      steps.map(([title, text]) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p set:html={text} />
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</Section>

<style>
  .path {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  li {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    padding-block: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-stretch: 110%;
    font-weight: 750;
    font-size: var(--size-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  p :global(code) {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    li {
      grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    p {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
